# Vesuva ("You may have this land enter tapped as a copy of any land on the battlefield") entering under Life and Limb and
# Humility. CR 614.12 judges each replacement effect that modifies how it enters on the permanent as it would exist on the
# battlefield, "taking into account replacement effects that have already modified how it enters". Before the copy, Vesuva is
# a land of no type - no Forest, no creature - so it keeps its own ability and becomes a copy of Overgrown Tomb. As that
# copy it is a Swamp Forest, which Life and Limb makes a 1/1 Saproling creature and Humility then takes the abilities of
# (CR 613.1f), so the copied "As this land enters, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters tapped" (CR 707.9a) no longer
# applies: Bot1 is not asked for life and stays at 20. It enters tapped by Vesuva's own replacement. The Overgrown Tomb itself
# asks nothing either (overgrown-tomb-entering-as-a-life-and-limb-creature-under-humility-asks-nothing-and-enters-untapped).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Life and Limb
Humility
Plains
Overgrown Tomb
Vesuva
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

